Dwarf valks are played disproportionatly by new players, so it's hard to
estimate how difficult they actually are; they have lower skill in
average going into the games.

It's hard to estimate the difficulty of wizards for a similar reason;
wizards are by far the most popular class for weird challenge runs, so
they tend to have fewer wins than would be expected if everyone were
trying to win.

I'm responsible for the statistics on the wiki; I attempted to control
for both factors by counting only games played immediately after the
person playing them had won twice in a row (and thus, was likely already
an experienced player, and likely wasn't trying for particularly
difficult conducts or challenges). Even so, though, it may be that the
second factor listed above is still having a noticeable effect on the
statistics.

